    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="5002d6ca-a434-5586-81ac-f87fe7530cf4" activityNameId="de6c481d-d518-53e2-a469-a90e9925ee24" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Ethylene carbonate, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Ethylene carbonate, at plant
The dataset can be used for example as electrolyt for batteries. Data are based on patents. For infrastructure, the ecoinvent dataset "chemical plant, organics" is accounted. Transportation efforts are based on ecoinvent standard estimates.;
CAS number: 000096-49-1; 
Formula: C3H4O3; 
Synonyms: 1,3-dioxolan-2-one; ethylene glycol carbonate; 
UUID: 8c478971-c3e4-3a3e-b017-706c11b12c55
This dataset includes the reaction of ethylene oxide with carbon dioxide in a reactor with a reaction temperatur at 120°C under pressure and with the use of a silver based catalyst. Energy consumption, ethylene oxide and CO2 emissions to air are calculated. After heating, process runs adiabatic.
Location: Some Swiss or European datasets are used for global processes.
Technology: This dataset includes a method of producing ethylene carbonate out of ethylene oxide and carbon dioxide  under adiabatic conditions (after heating). Temperature in the reactor: 120 - 130 °C; pressure: 16 bar. Ethylene oxide conversion is 99.95%. Assupmtion: Catalyst ist silver based.   
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: patent, ecoinvent 
Extrapolations: see Geography
Uncertainty adjustments: Uncertainty is assessed using the pedigree matrix.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_8c478971-c3e4-3a3e-b017-706c11b12c55.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
